# Website Project Rules

This website project should follow the patterns, conventions, and design system established in the Angel Tree Tracker application located at `/Users/mary/Documents/github/angel-tree-tracker`.

## ⚠️ STRICT Project Structure Requirements

**This project follows a strict folder structure. All new code MUST adhere to these rules.**

### Directory Structure Overview

```
src/
├── App.tsx                     # Root app with routing only
├── main.tsx                    # Entry point
├── index.css                   # Global styles & CSS variables
│
├── components/
│   ├── index.ts                # Master barrel export
│   │
│   ├── layout/                 # Site-wide layout components
│   │   ├── Header.tsx
│   │   ├── Footer.tsx
│   │   ├── PageWrapper.tsx
│   │   └── index.ts
│   │
│   ├── sections/               # Page sections (FEATURE-ORGANIZED)
│   │   ├── [section-name]/     # Each section gets its own folder
│   │   │   ├── ComponentName.tsx
│   │   │   ├── SubComponent.tsx  # Related sub-components
│   │   │   └── index.ts          # Barrel export
│   │   └── index.ts            # Re-exports all sections
│   │
│   ├── shared/                 # Reusable components across features
│   │   └── index.ts
│   │
│   └── ui/                     # shadcn/ui components ONLY
│       └── [component].tsx
│
├── hooks/                      # Custom React hooks
│   └── index.ts
│
├── lib/                        # Utility functions
│   └── utils.ts
│
├── pages/                      # Page components
│   ├── [PageName].tsx
│   └── index.ts
│
├── types/                      # TypeScript type definitions
│   └── index.ts
│
├── constants/                  # App constants and configuration
│   └── index.ts
│
├── contexts/                   # React Context providers (when needed)
│   └── index.ts
│
└── integrations/               # External service integrations (when needed)
    └── [service-name]/
```

### Section Component Rules

**CRITICAL: All page sections MUST follow this pattern:**

1. **Create a folder** for each section in `src/components/sections/`
   - Use kebab-case for folder names: `hero/`, `mission/`, `about-us/`
   
2. **Each section folder MUST contain:**
   - Main component file (PascalCase): `HeroBanner.tsx`
   - Barrel export: `index.ts`
   - Sub-components if needed: `RoleTile.tsx`, `FeatureCard.tsx`

3. **Example section structure:**
   ```
   sections/
   ├── hero/
   │   ├── HeroBanner.tsx       # Main section component
   │   ├── HeroContent.tsx      # Sub-component (if needed)
   │   └── index.ts             # export { HeroBanner } from './HeroBanner';
   │
   ├── features/
   │   ├── Features.tsx
   │   ├── FeatureCard.tsx      # Extracted sub-component
   │   └── index.ts
   │
   └── index.ts                 # Re-exports: export * from './hero'; etc.
   ```

4. **Barrel exports are MANDATORY:**
   ```typescript
   // sections/hero/index.ts
   export { HeroBanner } from './HeroBanner';
   
   // sections/index.ts
   export * from './hero';
   export * from './mission';
   export * from './features';
   ```

### Where to Put New Components

| Component Type | Location | Example |
|---------------|----------|---------|
| Page section | `components/sections/[name]/` | Hero, Mission, Features |
| Layout element | `components/layout/` | Header, Footer, Sidebar |
| Reusable UI | `components/shared/` | LoadingSpinner, Modal |
| shadcn/ui | `components/ui/` | Button, Card, Dialog |
| Page | `pages/` | Index.tsx, About.tsx |

### Import Conventions

**Preferred import style using barrel exports:**
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Import from barrel exports
import { HeroBanner, Mission, Features } from "@/components/sections";
import { Header, Footer } from "@/components/layout";

// ✅ ALSO GOOD - Import from specific section
import { HeroBanner } from "@/components/sections/hero";

// ❌ BAD - Direct file imports bypass barrel exports
import { HeroBanner } from "@/components/sections/hero/HeroBanner";
```

### Adding New Sections Checklist

When adding a new section, ALWAYS:

1. [ ] Create folder: `src/components/sections/[section-name]/`
2. [ ] Create main component: `[SectionName].tsx`
3. [ ] Create barrel export: `index.ts` with exports
4. [ ] Add to sections barrel: Update `src/components/sections/index.ts`
5. [ ] Extract sub-components if component exceeds ~150 lines
6. [ ] Import in page using barrel export

### Adding New Pages Checklist

When adding a new page, ALWAYS:

1. [ ] Create page component: `src/pages/[PageName].tsx`
2. [ ] Add to pages barrel: Update `src/pages/index.ts`
3. [ ] Add route: Update `src/App.tsx` with new route
4. [ ] Add route constant: Update `src/constants/index.ts` ROUTES object

### File Naming Conventions

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Components | PascalCase | `HeroBanner.tsx`, `FeatureCard.tsx` |
| Folders | kebab-case | `hero/`, `call-to-action/` |
| Hooks | camelCase with `use` prefix | `useScrollPosition.ts` |
| Utilities | camelCase | `utils.ts`, `formatDate.ts` |
| Types | camelCase or PascalCase | `types.ts`, `User.ts` |
| Constants | camelCase (SCREAMING_SNAKE for values) | `routes.ts`, `ROUTES.HOME` |

